Description: SSH3 client and server - SSH over QUIC/HTTP3 transport
 SSH3 in Go (the nagual2 fork of francoismichel/ssh3): the SSH3
 protocol carried over HTTP/3 (QUIC, RFC 9220 extended CONNECT).
 The package ships the ssh3 client and the ssh3-server daemon.
 .
 The client CLI follows the ssh(1) canon: sessions, the ssh2-shaped
 -L/-R/-D forwards (the documented udp:// extension), -J proxy
 jumps, the control master (-M/-S), the agent forwarding (-A), file
 transfers (ssh3 -transfer, the scp analog) and the -f background
 form; the fork's own long forms stay as deprecated aliases.
 .
 The daemon authenticates public keys (authorized_keys or
 .ssh3/authorized_identities of the target account) and, on amd64,
 passwords against the unix accounts (the CGO crypt backend,
 enabled by default; SSH3_ENABLE_PASSWORD_LOGIN=0 turns it off and
 the root account always refuses the password step).  Reverse
 forwards honor the GatewayPorts policy; the per-user limits
 (connections, channels, sftp sessions, reverse listeners) and the
 brute-force lockout are tunable through flags and SSH3_* variables
 read from /etc/ssh3/ssh3-server.env.
 .
 The binary package ssh3-go and the sibling C17 implementation
 package ssh3-server (source ssh3-c) conflict and replace each
 other in both directions: installing either one replaces the
 other's identical /usr/bin/ssh3 and /usr/bin/ssh3-server
 interfaces.
